; `pick c with F` finds its existential with the parts of a conjunction in any order, and with the
; written `-3 + k` against the derived `k + -3` (2026-10-15, todo 52): the derived `∃` of
; natural.kurt's "range" is compared normalized -- `- 3` is the number `-3` -- and a `sym` operator's
; arguments as a set.
load logic, natural
const y
calc on
use y ∈ { -3, ..., 8 }
show y <= 8
proof
    ∃ $k ∈ Nat (y = -3 + $k ∧ y <= 8)
    pick k with k ∈ Nat ∧ y = -3 + k ∧ y <= 8
        y <= 8
qed

; and not the fact as written when a declared `var` is in it: `use ∃ z (R z x)` with `var x` is
; `∀ x ∃ z (R z x)`, and one `c` with `R c x` for every `x` would be wrong -- the search accepted it
; for a moment on 2026-10-15, the kernel refused (the "false rejection" of todo 48 was a right one)
var x
const R
arity R 2
bool R 0
use ∃ z (R z x)
expect "ProofError"
    show ∃ w (R w x)
    proof
        pick c with R c x
            ∃ w (R w x)
    qed
